Silo patch 0009 — winegstreamer: the video decoder offers NV12 on macOS and refuses a Direct3D 11 manager
whose device can't make NV12 textures

Origin, part 1: Zagrios/voile-wine (Obelisk's Wine, itself built on crossover-sources-26.3.0), commit 8a10ac95
"winegstreamer: Decode to system memory when the Direct3D 11 device cannot make textures of the frames."
(2026-11-10, author Zagrios). License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, like Wine. Its hunks are carried unchanged.
Part 2 + 3 are Silo's, measured on FATAL FURY City of the Wolves (2492040) on 2026-11-14.

The problem, measured with +mfplat on FATAL FURY (Unreal Engine 5; its player drives the H.264 decoder MFT
directly, no media session) under D3DMetal, without Microsoft's Media Foundation DLLs:
  * the game sends MFT_MESSAGE_SET_D3D_MANAGER with a DXGI device manager, sets H.264 input, then lists the
    output types: YV12, YV12, IYUV, I420, YUY2 — no NV12, because CrossOver's CW HACK 26265 skips NV12 on
    macOS in transform_GetOutputAvailableType. It wants NV12, picks nothing and skips every movie.
  * With the hack gone it picks NV12; 8a10ac95 then sees that the device can't make NV12 textures (D3DMetal
    and DXMT can't) and drops the manager inside init_allocator, so frames come in system memory and nothing
    crashes. But the manager had been ACCEPTED, so the game stays on its hardware path, asks each output
    buffer for IMFDXGIBuffer, gets nothing and ends the stream.
  * Refusing the manager up front (MF_E_UNSUPPORTED_D3D_TYPE) sends the game down its software path:
    movies play (user-verified 2026-11-14).

What this patch does:
  1. 8a10ac95, unchanged: device_manager_holds_type() asks the device (CheckFormatSupport, never a texture —
     asking for one stops the process on D3DMetal) whether it has 2D textures of the output type; a
     SET_D3D_MANAGER after the output type is refused when it doesn't, and a manager given before the type
     is dropped in init_allocator, decoding to system memory.
  2. CW HACK 26265 removed (and its now-unused is_macos()): NV12 is offered again. What the hack guarded
     against — D3DMetal stopping the process on an NV12 texture — can no longer happen: the device is asked
     about NV12 and a manager without it is refused or dropped, so no NV12 texture is ever requested.
  3. A SET_D3D_MANAGER that arrives before any output type is checked against NV12
     (device_manager_holds_nv12()) and refused when the device lacks it.
A Direct3D 9 manager, a manager without a device and a device that does have the format are taken as before.

Not a fix for every movie: SOULCALIBUR VI (544750) still shows none without Microsoft's MF — it uses the
media session, and Wine's topology_loader_Load is a stub (measured the same day). Games in a Media
Foundation bottle use Microsoft's msmpeg2vdec and never reach this decoder.

Upstream: CW HACK 26265 is CrossOver's; 8a10ac95 is not in WineHQ. Rebase onto each new CrossOver source.

